    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`. All 3 tests pass: the existing logger test and 2 new ones in `tests/test_llm_client.py`.\n\n**One thing you might not expect:** the pinned openai 3.19.2 uses a library called `httpx2` for its HTTP layer, not `httpx`, and `httpx` isn't installed at all. So the code builds the HTTP client with openai's own `DefaultHttpxClient` and `Timeout` rather than importing `httpx`, and adds no dependencies.\n\nHow it meets the four requirements:\n1. **Timeouts:** connect is 5s; read, write and pool are 30s. The same setting goes on both the OpenAI client and the HTTP client, because OpenAI would otherwise apply its own default timeout to each request.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a request event hook on the HTTP client logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. Retries go through the same HTTP client, so each attempt is logged.\n4. **Transport:** when `transport` is given, it's passed to the HTTP client. When it's `None`, the default transport is used.\n\n**New tests:**\n- One checks that both clients get the right timeouts and that `max_retries` is 2.\n- The other uses a stub transport that returns 500 twice and then 200. It confirms the transport handles all 3 requests (1 original + 2 retries) and that the log shows exactly three INFO lines of `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`.\n- The retry test imports `httpx2` directly and switches off openai's retry delay by patching one of its private methods. So it may need updating if openai changes those internals."
  },
